---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  '<p><a href="https://dokploy.com/">Dokploy</a> is an open-source, self-hosted Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS) alternative to Vercel/Heroku/Coolify that runs on top of Docker and Traefik.</p>\n<h2>Deployment Strategies</h2>\n<p>You can deploy KoAkademy in Dokploy using either:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Zero-Downtime Docker Compose Stack (Recommended)</strong>: Deploys decoupled services (<code>app</code> for HTTP, <code>horizon</code> for background queues, <code>scheduler</code> for cron) with health-gated <code>start-first</code> updates, automated rollbacks, and tuned resource caps.</li>\n<li><strong>Individual Services</strong>: Deploys Dokploy managed databases (PostgreSQL &amp; Redis) alongside standalone Application services.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Method 1: Zero-Downtime Compose Stack Deployment (Recommended)</h2>\n<h3>How Zero-Downtime Deployments Work in Dokploy</h3>\n<p>By default, Docker Swarm and Compose stop the existing container before starting the new one (<code>order: stop-first</code>), resulting in a brief <code>502 Bad Gateway</code> error while the new container boots.</p>\n<p>To achieve seamless, zero-downtime updates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>order: start-first</code></strong>: Docker starts the new container replica alongside the current running container.</li>\n<li><strong>Container Healthcheck</strong>: The internal <code>healthcheck</code> script probes <code>/health</code> (and supervisor processes).</li>\n<li><strong>VIP Routing Gate</strong>: Dokploy and Traefik keep routing user traffic to the old container until the new container reports <code>healthy</code> over the configured monitoring period.</li>\n<li><strong>Automated Rollback</strong>: If the new container fails its health checks during the monitor period, the update rolls back immediately without dropping traffic.</li>\n<li><strong>Decoupled Workers</strong>: The web container runs with <code>HORIZON_IN_HTTP_CONTAINER=&quot;false&quot;</code>, while Horizon and the scheduler run as dedicated services so queuing is not duplicated during start-first web container rollovers.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Step 1: Create a Project in Dokploy</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to your Dokploy dashboard.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create Project</strong> and name it <code>koakademy</code>.</li>\n<li>Inside the project, click <strong>Create Service</strong> and select <strong>Compose</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Step 2: Configure Compose Stack</h3>\n<p>Paste the following production Compose specification into the <strong>Raw Compose</strong> editor:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-yaml">version: &quot;3.8&quot;\n\nservices:\n  app:\n    image: ghcr.io/yukazakiri/koakademy:latest\n    env_file:\n      - .env\n    environment:\n      HEALTHCHECK_PATH: /health\n      HORIZON_IN_HTTP_CONTAINER: &quot;false&quot;\n    volumes:\n      - app-storage:/app/storage\n    networks:\n      - koakademy\n    deploy:\n      replicas: 1\n      resources:\n        limits:\n          memory: 3G\n        reservations:\n          memory: 1536M\n      placement:\n        constraints:\n          - node.role == manager\n        max_replicas_per_node: 2\n      update_config:\n        parallelism: 1\n        delay: 0s\n        order: start-first\n        monitor: 120s\n        failure_action: rollback\n      rollback_config:\n        parallelism: 1\n        order: stop-first\n      restart_policy:\n        condition: any\n      endpoint_mode: vip\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [&quot;CMD&quot;, &quot;healthcheck&quot;]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      start_period: 60s\n      retries: 5\n    stop_grace_period: 30s\n\n  horizon:\n    image: ghcr.io/yukazakiri/koakademy:latest\n    env_file:\n      - .env\n    environment:\n      CONTAINER_MODE: horizon\n      AUTO_MIGRATE: &quot;false&quot;\n      RUN_OPTIMIZE: &quot;false&quot;\n      RUN_SCOUT_SETTINGS: &quot;false&quot;\n    volumes:\n      - app-storage:/app/storage\n    networks:\n      - koakademy\n    deploy:\n      replicas: 1\n      resources:\n        limits:\n          memory: 1G\n        reservations:\n          memory: 384M\n      placement:\n        constraints:\n          - node.role == manager\n      restart_policy:\n        condition: any\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [&quot;CMD&quot;, &quot;healthcheck&quot;]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      start_period: 60s\n      retries: 5\n    stop_grace_period: 30m\n\n  scheduler:\n    image: ghcr.io/yukazakiri/koakademy:latest\n    env_file:\n      - .env\n    environment:\n      CONTAINER_MODE: scheduler\n      AUTO_MIGRATE: &quot;false&quot;\n      RUN_OPTIMIZE: &quot;false&quot;\n      RUN_SCOUT_SETTINGS: &quot;false&quot;\n    volumes:\n      - app-storage:/app/storage\n    networks:\n      - koakademy\n    deploy:\n      replicas: 1\n      resources:\n        limits:\n          memory: 384M\n        reservations:\n          memory: 128M\n      placement:\n        constraints:\n          - node.role == manager\n      restart_policy:\n        condition: any\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [&quot;CMD&quot;, &quot;healthcheck&quot;]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      start_period: 60s\n      retries: 5\n    stop_grace_period: 30s\n\n  pgsql:\n    image: postgres:18-alpine\n    environment:\n      POSTGRES_DB: koakademy\n      POSTGRES_USER: koakademy\n      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${DB_PASSWORD:?Set DB_PASSWORD in .env}\n    volumes:\n      - pgsql-data:/var/lib/postgresql\n    networks:\n      - koakademy\n    deploy:\n      replicas: 1\n      resources:\n        limits:\n          memory: 512M\n        reservations:\n          memory: 128M\n      placement:\n        constraints:\n          - node.role == manager\n\n  redis:\n    image: redis:7-alpine\n    command:\n      - redis-server\n      - --maxmemory\n      - 384mb\n      - --maxmemory-policy\n      - noeviction\n    volumes:\n      - redis-data:/data\n    networks:\n      - koakademy\n    deploy:\n      replicas: 1\n      resources:\n        limits:\n          memory: 448M\n        reservations:\n          memory: 128M\n      placement:\n        constraints:\n          - node.role == manager\n\n  gotenberg:\n    image: gotenberg/gotenberg:8\n    networks:\n      - koakademy\n    deploy:\n      replicas: 1\n      resources:\n        limits:\n          memory: 512M\n        reservations:\n          memory: 128M\n\nvolumes:\n  app-storage:\n  pgsql-data:\n  redis-data:\n\nnetworks:\n  koakademy:\n    driver: overlay\n    attachable: true\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Step 3: Configure Environment Variables</h3>\n<p>Under the <strong>Environment</strong> tab in Dokploy, add your application configuration:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-ini">APP_NAME=&quot;KoAkademy&quot;\nAPP_ENV=&quot;production&quot;\nAPP_DEBUG=&quot;false&quot;\nAPP_URL=&quot;https://school.example.com&quot;\nAPP_KEY=&quot;base64:...&quot; # Generate with: php artisan key:generate --show\n\n# Database\nDB_CONNECTION=&quot;pgsql&quot;\nDB_HOST=&quot;pgsql&quot;\nDB_PORT=&quot;5432&quot;\nDB_DATABASE=&quot;koakademy&quot;\nDB_USERNAME=&quot;koakademy&quot;\nDB_PASSWORD=&quot;StrongDatabasePasswordHere&quot;\n\n# Redis Cache &amp; Queues\nCACHE_STORE=&quot;redis&quot;\nSESSION_DRIVER=&quot;redis&quot;\nQUEUE_CONNECTION=&quot;redis&quot;\nREDIS_HOST=&quot;redis&quot;\nREDIS_PORT=&quot;6379&quot;\nREDIS_PASSWORD=&quot;&quot;\nREDIS_DB=&quot;0&quot;\nREDIS_CACHE_DB=&quot;1&quot;\nREDIS_QUEUE_DB=&quot;2&quot;\nREDIS_PDF_QUEUE_DB=&quot;3&quot;\n\n# Concurrency &amp; Performance\nOCTANE_SERVER=&quot;frankenphp&quot;\nOCTANE_WORKERS=&quot;2&quot;\nOCTANE_MAX_REQUESTS=&quot;500&quot;\nHORIZON_ENABLED=&quot;true&quot;\nHORIZON_PROCESSES=&quot;1&quot;\nHORIZON_PDF_PROCESSES=&quot;1&quot;\nHORIZON_MEMORY=&quot;256&quot;\nHORIZON_PDF_MEMORY=&quot;512&quot;\nASSESSMENT_EXPORT_PROCESSES=&quot;1&quot;\nASSESSMENT_EXPORT_EVENT_PROCESSES=&quot;1&quot;\nASSESSMENT_EXPORT_WORKER_MEMORY=&quot;512&quot;\n\n# Production Hardening\nTELESCOPE_ENABLED=&quot;false&quot;\nPULSE_ENABLED=&quot;false&quot;\nNIGHTWATCH_ENABLED=&quot;false&quot;\nLOG_LEVEL=&quot;info&quot;\n\n# PDF Engine &amp; Storage\nGOTENBERG_URL=&quot;http://gotenberg:3000&quot;\nLARAVEL_PDF_DRIVER=&quot;gotenberg&quot;\nLARAVEL_PDF_PRODUCTION_DRIVER=&quot;gotenberg&quot;\nFILESYSTEM_DISK=&quot;public&quot;\n</code></pre>\n<div class="doc-callout doc-callout-tip">\n  <p class="doc-callout-label">Handling Quotes in Dokploy</p><p>Dokploy&#39;s environment editor sometimes persists strings with surrounding quotation marks (e.g. <code>&quot;false&quot;</code>). KoAkademy&#39;s container entrypoint automatically strips surrounding quotes at boot to ensure flags like <code>APP_DEBUG=false</code> or <code>AUTO_MIGRATE=true</code> parse as strict booleans.</p>\n</div><h3>Step 4: Domain &amp; SSL Routing</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>In Dokploy&#39;s <strong>Domains</strong> section, add your domain: <code>school.example.com</code>.</li>\n<li>Select service: <code>app</code>, container port: <code>8000</code>.</li>\n<li>Enable <strong>HTTPS / SSL Certificate</strong> via Let&#39;s Encrypt or Cloudflare.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Deploy</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Zero-Downtime Redeployment &amp; Upgrade Runbook</h2>\n<p>When pushing new code or pulling a new release image (such as <code>yukazaki/koakademy:edge-frankenphp</code> or a tagged release <code>ghcr.io/yukazakiri/koakademy:v1.24.0</code>):</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Trigger Redeploy in Dokploy</strong>: Click <strong>Redeploy</strong> in the Dokploy Compose service.</li>\n<li><strong>Start-First Rollout</strong>:<ul>\n<li>Docker Swarm starts the new <code>app</code> replica first.</li>\n<li>The new replica runs database migrations (<code>AUTO_MIGRATE=true</code>), warms caches, boots FrankenPHP and Inertia SSR.</li>\n<li>Swarm waits up to 60 seconds (<code>start_period</code>) for the health check endpoint <code>/health</code> to return HTTP <code>200</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Route Traffic</strong>:<ul>\n<li>Once healthy, Traefik routes incoming connections to the new container.</li>\n<li>The previous container is stopped gracefully (<code>stop_grace_period: 30s</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Independent Worker Updates</strong>:<ul>\n<li>The <code>horizon</code> and <code>scheduler</code> services update in parallel without causing web request downtime.</li>\n<li>Horizon workers finish active jobs before terminating (<code>stop_grace_period: 30m</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Method 2: Standalone Application with Dokploy Managed Databases</h2>\n<p>If you prefer using Dokploy&#39;s UI-managed databases with automated backups:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Create PostgreSQL</strong>:<ul>\n<li>Go to <strong>Databases</strong> → <strong>Create PostgreSQL</strong>.</li>\n<li>Set Database name: <code>koakademy</code>, Username: <code>koakademy</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Create Redis</strong>:<ul>\n<li>Go to <strong>Databases</strong> → <strong>Create Redis</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Deploy Gotenberg</strong>:<ul>\n<li>Create an <strong>Application</strong> service with image <code>gotenberg/gotenberg:8</code>. Expose port <code>3000</code> to internal network.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Deploy KoAkademy</strong>:<ul>\n<li>Create an <strong>Application</strong> service with Docker image <code>ghcr.io/yukazakiri/koakademy:latest</code>.</li>\n<li>Set internal container port to <code>8000</code>.</li>\n<li>Mount persistent volume: Host <code>/var/lib/dokploy/volumes/koakademy-storage</code> -&gt; Container <code>/app/storage</code>.</li>\n<li>Set healthcheck path to <code>/up</code>.</li>\n<li>Connect the environment variables pointing to the Dokploy PostgreSQL and Redis internal hosts.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Post-Installation Verification</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Once the build completes and Traefik routes traffic, navigate to <code>https://school.example.com/setup</code>.</li>\n<li>Complete the initial registration wizard to set up your school and admin credentials.</li>\n<li>Check the application status at <code>https://school.example.com/up</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Self-Hosting on Dokploy"
  path="/docs/self-hosting/dokploy"
  description="Deploy and operate KoAkademy using Dokploy's open-source PaaS on your own VPS."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
